   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "I think that, I believe that",
     "texto": [
      "In statements like **Acho que vai chover** (I think it's going to rain), **acho que** and **penso que** are usually followed by the indicative.",
      "To say that something seems likely, use **parece que**: **Parece que vai fazer sol** (it seems it's going to be sunny)."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Doubts and certainties",
     "texto": [
      "**Talvez** (maybe) and **se calhar** (maybe, very common in Portugal): **Se calhar tens razão** (maybe you're right).",
      "To say you're sure, say **tenho a certeza** (I'm certain). To say you're not, say **tenho dúvidas** (I have doubts)."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Agreeing",
     "texto": [
      "**Concordo** (I agree). **Não concordo** (I don't agree). The same as in Spanish."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
